content.text:
The degradation is confined to `/hotels`, and the extra time sits between search's outgoing call to rate and rate's own handling. Here is the root cause I'm reporting.

```json
{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "search",
      "fault_kind": "http_slow",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, attr_span_kind k, count(*) n, round(avg(duration)/1e6,2) avg_ms, round(max(duration)/1e6,1) max_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name IN ('search','rate') GROUP BY ALL ORDER BY 1,2", "claim": "search's client span to rate.Rate/GetRates averages about 1926 ms, while rate's server span stays around 0.5 ms."},
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, attr_span_kind k, count(*) n, round(avg(duration)/1e6,2) avg_ms, round(max(duration)/1e6,1) max_ms FROM normal_traces WHERE service_name IN ('search','rate') GROUP BY ALL ORDER BY 1,2", "claim": "In the normal period search's client span to rate averages about 3 ms, so the gap is new in the incident."},
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT round(c.duration/1e6,1) client_ms, round(s.duration/1e6,2) server_ms, round((c.duration - s.duration)/1e6,1) gap_ms FROM abnormal_traces c JOIN abnormal_traces s ON c.span_id = s.parent_span_id WHERE c.service_name='search' AND c.span_name='rate.Rate/GetRates' ORDER BY client_ms DESC LIMIT 30", "claim": "Top slow search→rate calls show about 1.8–2.9 s of gap with sub-millisecond server time."},
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, attr_span_kind k, count(*) n, round(avg(duration)/1e6,2) avg_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='search' AND span_name='geo.Geo/Nearby' GROUP BY ALL", "claim": "search's other outgoing call, geo.Geo/Nearby, stays fast at about 0.44 ms, so the slowdown is specific to the rate call."}
      ]
    }
  ],
  "propagation": [
    {"from": "search", "to": "frontend", "evidence": [{"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, attr_span_kind k, count(*) n, round(avg(duration)/1e6,2) avg_ms, round(max(duration)/1e6,1) max_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE (service_name='frontend' AND span_name IN ('HTTP /hotels','search.Search/Nearby')) OR (service_name='search' AND span_name='search.Search/Nearby') GROUP BY ALL", "claim": "search.Search/Nearby server spans average about 1926 ms, and frontend's HTTP /hotels rises to about 1935 ms with it."}]}
  ]
}
```

The user-visible impact is limited to `/hotels` on `frontend`. Its latency rises from about 7.5 ms to about 1.9 s, and the other frontend paths stay normal. The chain runs from search to the user-facing frontend.

The kind is `http_slow` rather than `network_delay` because no per-connection network metrics show a problem. There are no `hubble_*` series in this case, and network errors, container CPU, memory and pod restarts are all flat. The delay sits in the caller's client span, before rate's own handling starts.
